codelaw-rules-python

data/python/stdlib.json lists the top-level module names of the Python
standard library: the union of `sys.stdlib_module_names` from CPython 3.10,
3.11, 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14 (https://www.python.org), released under the Python
Software Foundation License Version 2 (PSF-2.0). Copyright (c) 2001 Python
Software Foundation; All Rights Reserved.

The rules are reimplementations written for codelaw. Their `ported_from:`
fields name the Ruff rules (https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/, version 0.17.1, MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2022 Charles Marsh) whose documented behaviour they
reproduce; Ruff's rules in turn reimplement Pyflakes (MIT), pycodestyle
(MIT/Expat), flake8-bugbear (MIT) and isort (MIT). No code or documentation
text from any of them is included.
